Anna (docs): Quick ask 1: Updating the Aurora-lite3b model card to clarify input/sequence limits and show an SDK snippet for graceful truncation+retry. Users keep hitting unclear 413 errors. Can owners chime in with exact limits and a tiny snippet?

Ravi (eng-runtime): TL;DR: hosted Aurora-lite3b generate endpoints accept up to 4096 total tokens (prompt + generation). Embeddings endpoints accept up to 2048 input tokens. If a request exceeds the limit we return 413 with body {error: 'sequence_too_long', limit: <n>}. We'll add that exact response shape to the card.

Mei (eng-ml): Bench note to include: under typical single-GPU serving p50 generate latency for 1k prompt tokens ~180ms, p95 ~420ms (q4_0 variant, eu-west). Also call out that long prompts increase chance of cold-start amplification when batch windows are used.

Max (sdk): Snippet draft (JS) to surface client-side truncation + retry:
```js
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });
async function safeGenerate(prompt){
  try{
    return await client.generate({model:'aurora-lite3b', prompt});
  }catch(e){
    if(e.status===413 && e.body?.error==='sequence_too_long'){
      const limit = e.body.limit || 4096;
      const truncated = truncatePromptTo(prompt, limit-256); // leave room for generation
      return client.generate({model:'aurora-lite3b', prompt: truncated});
    }
    throw e;
  }
}
```

Max (sdk): Curl example for fallback: `curl -X POST /v1/generate -d '{"model":"aurora-lite3b","prompt":"..."}'` and check for 413 to trigger client truncation.

